{color:#ff5630}*ATTENTION!*{color}

{color:#ff5630}Any changes made to this Test Case needs to be reflected in {color}[https://igel-jira.atlassian.net/browse/QCAPPS-228|https://igel-jira.atlassian.net/browse/QCAPPS-228|smart-link]  {color:#ff5630}too!{color}
{color:#ff5630}Both check the very same feature. This Test Case does cover the feature from the OS perspective. The linked feature above covers it from the Apps perspective. Test are made the same way but keep the perspective in mind while digging for bugs.{color}

*Summary*

With the feature CUPS LPD the IGEL endpoint becomes a print server using the LPD printing protocol.
This service can be used by other endpoints which don’t have the possibility to use modern CUPS printer sharing.

*Environment*

*Helpful Terminal Comments*

*Additional information*

