h3. {color:#bf2600}No environment to test this complex walmart feature. We can only check the logs of the client, except for feature sessions.xlock0.options.login_feature3{color}

h3.

As an addition from 12.7.4 on, it is possible to send some more DHCP data to the client (client needs to request also additional data from DHCP):
You can check this with tcpdump and unplug/plug LAN cable.

* option igelrmserver code 224 text;
* option igelrmserver-port code 227 text;
* option igelrmserver-auth code 228 text;
* option igelrmserver-ca-hash code 229 text;

The igelrmserver-auth contains the mass-deployment key configured in the UMS, in case of mass-deplyment key the string must have the following format: “password:<YOUR_MASS_DEPLOYMENT_KEY>“.
The optional igelrmserver-ca-hash contains the hash (= fingerprint) of the root CA certificate of the TLS certificate chain used in the UMS for serving Web or ICG port.

The igelrmserver-port is optional, by default the 8443 is assumed.


Also there is a new debian server with isc-dhcp-server installed available. This dhcp server should be able to do exactly the same as the windows server 2019 DHCP. Of course only one DHCP server is allowed to run.

*Additional Information*

* Once opened, Kiosk can not be closed again without reboot. Therefore it is advisable to create a toolbar item of the type “custom” and have the following command as “Command to exectue”. This allows to close the Kiosk App without rebooting the whole system. The old method of running Kiosk App from the terminal with a command does not work anymore (without extensive prework).

{noformat}/bin/killall igel-secure-kiosk{noformat}

