This Test Case tests if the automatic login via SSO Identity Providers works in the Browser



*Additional Information*

* After a fresh installation of the Chromium Browser, Chromium needs to be started at least once before SSO credentials are passed-through from the IGEL OS. This is due to the Chromium profile with the configs necessary for it to work is created upon the very first start of the app. It therefore lacks all the configs at that point. Once it was started the first time, on subsequent start of the app it will pull the configs and the pass-through of the SSO credentials will work.
* Test Test Step “Clearance of Data after User logout” can only be tested on Edge for now. Other browsers do not have this feature yet. It may be added in the future.



{color:#ff5630}_Test Case Review Instructiions_{color}

{color:#ff5630}_We do not test the sync between MS Cloud Services for the “Clearance of Data after User logout” Test Step. Theoretically, all user data can be synced to MS Cloud services. Once the user logs out and in again, all this data should be transferred from MS Cloud onto the device. This requires a specifically configured user. We do not have such a user, but PO said, that testing this specific aspect is not required by QA._{color}

